            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GRAMMA GORGEOUS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a very easy, tasty bar. Not a lot to it. Be careful not to overbake. I used a 9x13 pan and the bars are quite thin. I didn't have golden syrup, so I used white syrup."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MC"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The secret to keeping the bars/cookies from crumbling is to use a small metal or hard rubber spatula to press the oat mixture *firmly* into the pan. I also recommend cutting the bars while warm, then letting them cool completely in the pan. My family loves raisins and a slightly more chewy texture, so I added (1) cup to the mix.",
            "datePublished": "2018-10-07T19:58:52.330Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tara Mom to 2"
            },
            "reviewBody": "After a vacation in South Africa where I became addicted to a cookie bar like this sold in the Kruger National Park shops, I was determined to find a recipe. This is close enough to be a keeper. We have now made it at least 3 times, and will continue to make it. So yummy with a cup of tea. I make them in a glass 9x9 pan lined with parchment, and use more parchment to press them into place.",
            "datePublished": "2019-03-12T15:29:17.383Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shareen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are simple to make and taste great! \n\nI did make an adjustment, as I had no golden syrup. I used honey instead. \n\nI also baked it for five minutes more due to the high altitude.\n\nI printed and saved this one to my recipe folder :)",
            "datePublished": "2017-05-02T00:09:44.360Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "shannon"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a delicious crumbly mess! I will never make it again. I guess I didn’t press it into the pan firmly enough. I substituted agave syrup for corn syrup.",
            "datePublished": "2020-12-20T20:41:30.177Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nadezna Walsh"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It looks great in the oven",
            "datePublished": "2012-09-21T19:25:27.230Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Laura A"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My batch should have been called Crumblers instead of Crunchers. While I give this 5 stars for flavor I give it 1 star for texture. My bars were extremely dry and fragile. I followed measurements precisely but I used unsweetened coconut which does not seem as moist as sweetened coconut. I also substituted a mix of honey and corn syrup for the golden syrup. Perhaps that affected the moisture as well? Anyway - - it made very yummy crumbs.",
            "datePublished": "2009-12-18T17:48:56.173Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AK Schmied"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I baked them for 15 min. and they looked white at the middle so i baked for 10 min more. And this probably made them too dry. \n\nOh another mistake, don't put more than 1 cup coconut flake coz that'll be too much! I had 1 1/2 cup so i didn't know what to do with the rest 1/2 cup so i put altogether and i think...it's not good.\n\nso i think next time i will bake them in an 9*13 pan and not take out from the oven since 15 min..let's see how they will turn out.\n\nbut they still taste good...",
            "datePublished": "2006-01-16T00:57:24.187Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I like my anzac biscuits to be softer, so tried this out. Unsure if I measured wrong, but the mixture seemed too dry, so my over zealous boy friend decided to add too much water. They still turned out great though.",
            "datePublished": "2005-03-28T12:49:55.967Z"
          },
